@flexiarg task-selection/serves-a-way
@title Serves a Way
@keywords placement, way, action, work
@audience agents and the War Machine selecting the next task
@tone design
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-11-02 (codex-12 for claude-2)
@role gate
@guard placement: the cited line and way(s) served, action, and open status.
@effect keeps candidates placed under a way with action work.
@predicts the selected task's reason names the way it serves.
@references [task-selection/only-what-can-start-now task-selection/what-others-wait-on-first]
! conclusion: Keep work placed under a cited way and name that way in the reason.

  + context: Ant placements connect open tasks to the ways they serve.

  + IF:
    A ready candidate has an open placement under one or more cited ways.

  + HOWEVER:
    Audit, held, close, absent, and empty-way placements are not work placements.

  + THEN:
    Keep only placements whose action is work or a named work cluster.

  + BECAUSE:
    A dispatch should say which way the selected work serves.
